 If the property is not defined in any parent dataset, it is removed entirely.
 Property values are limited to 8192 bytes.
+.Ss QoS User Properties
+The following user properties are recognized by the QoS (Quality of Service)
+I/O rate limiting subsystem.
+They control per-dataset I/O throttling via a dual token bucket
+(IOPS and bandwidth).
+These properties are inherited by child datasets.
+Setting a rate to
+.Sy 0
+disables QoS limiting for that dataset.
+.Bl -tag -width "qos:max_iops_write"
+.It Sy qos:max_iops_read
+Maximum read I/O operations per second (integer).
+Each read I/O consumes one IOPS token regardless of size.
+.It Sy qos:max_iops_write
+Maximum write I/O operations per second (integer).
+Each write I/O consumes one IOPS token regardless of size.
+.It Sy qos:max_bw_read
+Maximum read I/O bandwidth in bytes per second (integer).
+Each read I/O consumes tokens equal to its size in bytes.
+.It Sy qos:max_bw_write
+Maximum write I/O bandwidth in bytes per second (integer).
+Each write I/O consumes tokens equal to its size in bytes.
+.It Sy qos:max_iosize
+Maximum allowed I/O size in bytes (integer).
+I/Os larger than this value are rejected with
+.Er EIO .
+Set to
+.Sy 0
+for no limit.
+.El
+.Pp
+Example:
+.Bd -literal -offset indent
+zfs set qos:max_bw_read=104857600 tank/client-001     # 100 MB/s read
+zfs set qos:max_bw_write=52428800 tank/client-001     # 50 MB/s write
+zfs set qos:max_iops_read=5000 tank/client-001
+zfs set qos:max_iops_write=3000 tank/client-001
+zfs set qos:max_iosize=131072 tank/client-001          # 128K
+zfs set qos:max_bw_read=0 tank/client-001              # disable read limit
+zfs inherit qos:max_bw_read tank/client-001            # inherit from parent
+.Ed
+.Ss QoS Module Parameters
+The following module parameters control system-wide QoS behavior and can
+be read and modified at runtime via
+.Pa /sys/module/zfs/parameters/ :
+.Bl -tag -width "zfs_qos_read_timeout_ms"
+.It Sy zfs_qos_read_timeout_ms
+Maximum time in milliseconds a throttled read I/O will wait for tokens
+before returning
+.Er EIO
+(default:
+.Sy 10000 ,
+effective floor:
+.Sy 100 ) .
+For NFS soft-mount clients, set this value below the client
+.Sy timeo
+parameter so ZFS abandons the wait before the NFS client issues its own
+.Er EIO .
+.Bd -literal -offset indent
+# Align with NFS timeo=80 (8 s)
+echo 7000 | sudo tee /sys/module/zfs/parameters/zfs_qos_read_timeout_ms
+.Ed
+.El
